# Changelog
- Vendored dev86 toolchain into the project for portability to make builds
  easier.
- Original MINIX Makefiles updated to use dev86 toolchain. Top-level makefile
  added.
- Added bcc compiler helper methods to MINIX libc to satisfy the linker.
- Assembly comments ported to as86: `|` -> `;`/`!`/
- Renamed a few assembly macros that clash with keywords in as86.
- `jmp` assembly instructions replaced with `jmp near` when 16-bit jmp needed.
- `out`/`in` assembly instructions ported to as86 `outb`/`inb`.
- Made minimal changes to crtso.s, head.s and end.s for compatibility with
  dev86 toolchain.
- Fixed a couple of breaking typos in MINIX sources discovered during builds.
- Ported boot MINIX diskette `build.c` program to Python to make bootable MINIX
  disk images from the host machine.
- Removed unneeded begtext, begdata, begbss, endtext, enddata, endbss labels
  from bootblok.s. `asld` might have needed these, but `as86 -b` complains.
- Updated bootblok makefile comment since as86 generates different (but
  equivalent) opcodes for `xor si,si` and `xor di,di` instructions.
- as86 doesn't always respect the .bss directive and assembles some .bss
  declared symbols from the MINIX assembly source code into the data segment.
  Depending on how the stack is defined, this can break things. Fixed this
  by adding .comm assembly directives to some MINIX assembly source code.
- Replaced `end.s` with __endtext, __edata, and __end labels provided by ld86
  to fix initial _brksize value.
- Fixed bug in chmem code when dealing with non-I&D programs.
